@@ -9,6 +9,16 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+Client navigation keeps the five most recently used inactive page views in a
+hidden, inert container. Returning to a cached URL restores the original DOM and
+React island state, including unfinished form input. Query strings identify
+separate views; hash links share a view. Astro still fetches each destination and
+updates its head, history, and scroll position normally. Cached page content stays
+as it was left until eviction or a full reload; it is not refreshed from that fetch.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for automated DOM cache checks and `pnpm build` for the production
+build.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
